OK.

750
00:42:35,800 --> 00:42:36,920
Yeah.
Trust you.

751
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:38,080
Yeah.
OK.

752
00:42:41,160 --> 00:42:44,760
You're, like, the one
that I actually am...legit trust.

753
00:42:44,760 --> 00:42:45,800
Yes?

754
00:42:45,800 --> 00:42:48,040
Shonee's talking to Kirby right now.

755
00:42:48,040 --> 00:42:51,720
Someone's got to go and get in
on that Shonee conversation.

756
00:42:51,720 --> 00:42:53,040
They want George.

757
00:42:53,040 --> 00:42:54,800
Really?
They want all on George.

758
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:56,280
Really?

759
00:42:58,080 --> 00:42:59,480
OK.

760
00:43:01,680 --> 00:43:05,600
GEORGE: The longer this scramble has
gone, the more worried I'm getting,

761
00:43:05,600 --> 00:43:08,400
because all I hear
is myself coming up as an option.

762
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:13,080
So, I need to make sure

763
00:43:13,080 --> 00:43:17,440
that somebody who isn't King George
of Bankstown goes home.

764
00:43:27,360 --> 00:43:28,680
What do you guys think?

765
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:31,480
Come in, Luke.

766
00:43:32,960 --> 00:43:35,680
What would make you happy, Luke?
Honestly.

767
00:43:35,680 --> 00:43:39,160
If Janine goes,
does that make you happy?

768
00:43:39,160 --> 00:43:40,240
Uh...

769
00:43:44,440 --> 00:43:45,680
Mm-hm.
Um...

770
00:43:45,680 --> 00:43:47,280
If youse want to vote J,
I'll vote J.

771
00:43:47,280 --> 00:43:49,280
We all just dump on Janine.

772
00:43:51,200 --> 00:43:53,840
I'm taking control of the situation.

773
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:57,480
Vote off Janine and there's no
crying over spilt milk.

774
00:43:57,480 --> 00:43:59,600
Janine goes home.
Is that a problem for you?

775
00:43:59,600 --> 00:44:01,480
No, that's not a problem for me.
Is that OK for you?

776
00:44:01,480 --> 00:44:06,360
Am I reinventing the wheel
with an "anyone but me" strategy? No.

777
00:44:06,360 --> 00:44:10,560
But I've made sure I'm not
the first boot on this tribe.

778
00:44:14,400 --> 00:44:15,760
Fine.

779
00:44:23,120 --> 00:44:24,680
Always bet on black.

780
00:44:24,680 --> 00:44:26,160
Or gold.

781
00:45:01,280 --> 00:45:02,960
Go ahead. Grab a torch.

782
00:45:02,960 --> 00:45:05,880
Come forward, dip it in and get fire.

783
00:45:08,600 --> 00:45:10,160
GEORGE: Doing this again.

784
00:45:12,720 --> 00:45:14,880
It's part of the ritual
of Tribal Council,

785
00:45:14,880 --> 00:45:18,120
because in this game,
fire represents your life.

786
00:45:20,680 --> 00:45:21,960
Once it's gone...

787
00:45:23,960 --> 00:45:25,560
..so are you.

788
00:45:32,960 --> 00:45:35,960
So, George, what do you think?

789
00:45:35,960 --> 00:45:37,880
Do you like
what we've done with the place?

790
00:45:37,880 --> 00:45:42,160
It seems familiar,
but different at the same time.

791
00:45:42,160 --> 00:45:45,520
But given I come to Tribal Council
so often,

792
00:45:45,520 --> 00:45:47,480
I was hoping for two nights off
in a row.

793
00:45:47,480 --> 00:45:49,640
But that never happens for me,
does it?

794
00:45:52,280 --> 00:45:55,680
Kirby, your season,
you had a lot of chaos,

795
00:45:55,680 --> 00:45:58,280
so you should be at home right here.

796
00:45:58,280 --> 00:46:01,520
Yeah... Oh, I feel like
that's just amateur league

797
00:46:01,520 --> 00:46:03,000
in comparison to this.

798
00:46:04,920 --> 00:46:07,040
They're professionals in every way,

799
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:10,280
and I feel like I'm amongst
kings, queens and gods,

800
00:46:10,280 --> 00:46:12,160
and I'm the princess
amongst them all.

801
00:46:12,160 --> 00:46:13,720
So...
OK. (LAUGHS)

802
00:46:15,000 --> 00:46:17,640
Like, they're elite at this game,

803
00:46:17,640 --> 00:46:20,280
and I love watching them
do what they do,

804
00:46:20,280 --> 00:46:23,520
and they're so charming
and sweet and embracing,

805
00:46:23,520 --> 00:46:26,640
and you just think, "Yes,
I'm with you, I trust you,"

806
00:46:26,640 --> 00:46:28,560
and then you think about it
and you're like, "What...

807
00:46:28,560 --> 00:46:30,600
"What were they just saying?"

808
00:46:30,600 --> 00:46:32,720
So, they're really good.

809
00:46:32,720 --> 00:46:35,680
Uh...Kirbs, I don't think
you should be

810
00:46:35,680 --> 00:46:38,480
retracting yourself
from the same hill

811
00:46:38,480 --> 00:46:42,520
because you were playing pretty big
today, in my opinion,

812
00:46:42,520 --> 00:46:44,800
and I think you play this game
very, very well.

813
00:46:44,800 --> 00:46:46,720
So to try and take yourself
out of the equation...

814
00:46:46,720 --> 00:46:48,480
I'm still the princess.

815
00:46:51,320 --> 00:46:54,480
I actually think Kirby is playing
one of the best games.

816
00:46:56,200 --> 00:46:58,600
The way she's playing is...
like, it's amazing.

817
00:46:58,600 --> 00:47:01,840
Not rattled at all. Super calm.
People coming to chat.

818
00:47:04,320 --> 00:47:07,120
Like, people are looking to her
for what's going to happen tonight.

819
00:47:13,200 --> 00:47:16,240
George, there are a lot of
connections in this tribe.

820
00:47:16,240 --> 00:47:19,920
It's almost like a Venn diagram
of who's played with who, right?

821
00:47:19,920 --> 00:47:24,000
Yeah. It's a...it's a tribe
with an interesting dynamic.

822
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:26,920
And I feel like the problem
that this tribe has had

823
00:47:26,920 --> 00:47:29,920
after three days
of seven Australian legends together

824
00:47:29,920 --> 00:47:32,160
is we have competing priorities,

825
00:47:32,160 --> 00:47:36,040
and how you balance those
priorities, um...

826
00:47:36,040 --> 00:47:41,200
(GEORGE CONTINUES TALKING,
AUDIO MUTED)

827
00:47:41,200 --> 00:47:42,680
..you've got to take into account

828
00:47:42,680 --> 00:47:45,800
in a couple of days we merge,
and then we're at endgame.

829
00:47:51,400 --> 00:47:53,520
Wow. David, that...that was a lot.

830
00:47:53,520 --> 00:47:54,920
Wait, what?
(OTHERS LAUGH)

831
00:47:54,920 --> 00:47:57,640
Did you...did you hear any of that?

832
00:47:57,640 --> 00:48:00,200
(CONVERSATION CONTINUES
IN BACKGROUND)

833
00:48:16,200 --> 00:48:18,400
Janine, is that how fast
the game is now?

834
00:48:18,400 --> 00:48:21,440
JANINE: Oh, yeah. It's...it's like,
um, Survivor on steroids.

835
00:48:23,560 --> 00:48:26,520
It was like "bang!" into it,
and it's like, "Whoa." (LAUGHS)

836
00:48:32,600 --> 00:48:36,280
So, Sarah, it's been like
seven years since you last played.

837
00:48:36,280 --> 00:48:38,920
Yeah.
How different does this feel?

838
00:48:38,920 --> 00:48:42,000
Yeah, you definitely feel like
you're playing with professionals

839
00:48:42,000 --> 00:48:44,400
when you're playing Aus v World.

840
00:48:44,400 --> 00:48:46,240
Like, it's straight into it.

841
00:48:46,240 --> 00:48:47,800
But I'm trying a new tactic.

842
00:48:51,200 --> 00:48:54,960
I was a little bit cheeky sneaky
last time I played.

843
00:48:54,960 --> 00:48:56,960
I'm trying to go with
this loyalty thing.

844
00:48:56,960 --> 00:48:58,720
See how it works for me.

845
00:49:05,040 --> 00:49:07,400
Luke, do you feel like
it's any different for you?

846
00:49:07,400 --> 00:49:10,160
Uh, no, not really.

847
00:49:10,160 --> 00:49:11,640
I think it's like riding a bike.

848
00:49:11,640 --> 00:49:15,080
I think we still lie and cheat
and steal, really.

849
00:49:15,080 --> 00:49:20,240
It's the same game, but, uh,
maybe a little bit faster, this one.

850
00:49:20,240 --> 00:49:25,000
I think we're going to experience
that throughout this whole game.

851
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:26,840
(LUKE CONTINUES TALKING,
AUDIO FADES)

852
00:49:35,160 --> 00:49:37,200
There was names getting
thrown around at the start,

853
00:49:37,200 --> 00:49:39,120
and then it changed again.

854
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:41,720
Um, it's seriously...
Like, look at it right now.

855
00:49:41,720 --> 00:49:43,320
It's a live tribal.

856
00:49:45,680 --> 00:49:47,520
Things can change here.

857
00:49:48,720 --> 00:49:50,240
Right here. Like...

858
00:49:50,240 --> 00:49:52,760
So, whatever happens at the beach
probably means nothing,

859
00:49:52,760 --> 00:49:55,200
because what's gonna
happen here is...

860
00:49:55,200 --> 00:49:56,880
..is going to change again.

861
00:49:56,880 --> 00:49:59,680
There certainly is
a lot of whispering going on

862
00:49:59,680 --> 00:50:01,520
down that end of the tribe.

863
00:50:06,680 --> 00:50:11,640
In fairness, we kind of went, "Aaah!
Right, what's going on?"

864
00:50:19,520 --> 00:50:21,120
So, Janine, are things changing?

865
00:50:21,120 --> 00:50:23,640
Mate, it's frickin' Survivor,
isn't it?

866
00:50:23,640 --> 00:50:26,000
So, you know, I...I get...

867
00:50:26,000 --> 00:50:29,360
..I get awfully confused
about what's going on.

868
00:50:29,360 --> 00:50:31,520
It's the first Tribal,

869
00:50:31,520 --> 00:50:33,600
and no-one knows
where everyone really sits.

870
00:50:33,600 --> 00:50:36,400
You know, we've had conversations,
we've had certain things.

871
00:50:36,400 --> 00:50:38,560
You...you go talk, then. Go talk.

872
00:50:38,560 --> 00:50:39,640
(LAUGHS)

873
00:51:08,920 --> 00:51:09,960
Like, if you're down...

874
00:51:13,880 --> 00:51:15,080
Yeah. OK.

875
00:51:15,080 --> 00:51:16,240
That seems like...

876
00:52:13,160 --> 00:52:14,280
OK.

877
00:52:32,160 --> 00:52:35,560
So, Kirby, there was a clear split
in the discussions...

878
00:52:38,160 --> 00:52:39,320
..right there.

879
00:52:39,320 --> 00:52:41,720
Does that... Is that indicative of
what's going on in the tribe

880
00:52:41,720 --> 00:52:43,040
in terms of alliances?

881
00:52:44,200 --> 00:52:46,640
Don't ask me. The Kings and God
just went and spoke,

882
00:52:46,640 --> 00:52:49,240
and I don't know what about
because they've been at each other.

883
00:52:54,520 --> 00:52:57,000
I don't know - I think it's always
good to keep your options open.

884
00:52:58,280 --> 00:53:00,640
And there's one thing to be,
like, hiding on the beach

885
00:53:00,640 --> 00:53:02,080
or scurrying around the beach is...

886
00:53:02,080 --> 00:53:04,720
(DAVID CONTINUES TALKING,
AUDIO FADES)

887
00:53:18,440 --> 00:53:21,760
So how many conversations
were you part of this afternoon?

888
00:53:21,760 --> 00:53:23,360
A lot.

889
00:53:23,640 --> 00:53:25,840
I think a lot of names
got floated today,

890
00:53:25,840 --> 00:53:27,240
so that makes people nervous.

891
00:53:27,240 --> 00:53:29,080
I know my name
was getting floated today

892
00:53:29,080 --> 00:53:30,960
and that made me very nervous.

893
00:53:33,280 --> 00:53:36,120
Shonee, given your experience
at Tribal Council,

894
00:53:36,120 --> 00:53:38,440
you must have a sense of
where the vote's going tonight.

895
00:53:41,560 --> 00:53:45,080
Honestly, like, coming in here
and just, like, looking around...

896
00:53:45,080 --> 00:53:46,800
(SHONEE CONTINUES TALKING,
AUDIO FADES)

897
00:53:48,000 --> 00:53:49,960
And I feel like I'm coming in and...

898
00:53:49,960 --> 00:53:51,280
(AUDIO FADES)

899
00:53:53,800 --> 00:53:55,720
..I've played with
two people before.

900
00:53:55,720 --> 00:53:58,400
They both voted me off.
That's a great start.

901
00:53:58,400 --> 00:54:02,240
But what I offer is a clean slate
to the others.

902
00:54:02,240 --> 00:54:03,800
And also... (AUDIO FADES)

903
00:54:25,960 --> 00:54:28,280
So, Luke,
what's tonight's vote about for you?

904
00:54:28,280 --> 00:54:31,920
Ooh. That is a very good question.

905
00:54:33,440 --> 00:54:38,520
Uh, as...as simple as to put it,
is about how I'm moving forward

906
00:54:38,520 --> 00:54:41,120
and who I want to move forward with.

907
00:54:42,320 --> 00:54:43,800
So...
Agreed.

908
00:54:43,800 --> 00:54:46,360
Because inasmuch as this
is an individual game,

909
00:54:46,360 --> 00:54:52,160
you sometimes do need people
to actually have your interests,

910
00:54:52,160 --> 00:54:53,960
uh, to move forward.

911
00:54:56,280 --> 00:54:58,280
That's how I like to play.

912
00:54:58,280 --> 00:55:01,920
Definitely have your guys back
when you say you have their back.

913
00:55:04,800 --> 00:55:07,920
I like it. It's a good answer.
Let's see who's got whose back.

914
00:55:07,920 --> 00:55:09,600
It is time to vote.

915
00:55:09,600 --> 00:55:11,080
David, you're up.

916
00:55:11,080 --> 00:55:12,320
Oof.

917
00:56:26,160 --> 00:56:27,840
(CLEARS THROAT)

918
00:56:49,760 --> 00:56:51,560
I'll go count the votes.

919
00:57:10,760 --> 00:57:13,360
Alright. If anyone has an idol
and you want to play it,

920
00:57:13,360 --> 00:57:15,360
now would be the time to do so.

921
00:57:33,280 --> 00:57:34,520
I'll read the votes.

922
00:57:40,480 --> 00:57:42,480
First vote, Janine.

923
00:57:48,560 --> 00:57:49,880
George.

924
00:57:57,880 --> 00:57:59,000
George.

925
00:58:03,360 --> 00:58:06,240
Two votes George, one vote Janine.

926
00:58:09,520 --> 00:58:10,800
George.

927
00:58:12,880 --> 00:58:17,480
That's three votes George,
one vote Janine.

928
00:58:22,800 --> 00:58:23,840
David.

929
00:58:31,720 --> 00:58:32,880
David.

930
00:58:37,840 --> 00:58:40,080
Three votes George,
two votes David,

931
00:58:40,080 --> 00:58:41,400
one vote Janine.

932
00:58:44,040 --> 00:58:45,280
One vote left.

933
00:58:52,480 --> 00:58:54,200
David. We're tied.

934
00:59:17,400 --> 00:59:21,160
Three votes George,
two votes David, one vote Janine.

935
00:59:21,160 --> 00:59:22,600
One vote left.

936
00:59:27,280 --> 00:59:29,120
David. We're tied.

937
00:59:32,200 --> 00:59:35,720
Alright, we're gonna revote.
This is how it's going to work.

938
00:59:35,720 --> 00:59:38,680
George and David,
you will not vote.

939
00:59:38,680 --> 00:59:42,360
Everyone else, you can only
vote for George or David.

940
00:59:46,800 --> 00:59:47,920
Sarah, you're up.

941
01:00:27,640 --> 01:00:29,520
I'll go count the votes.

942
01:00:41,600 --> 01:00:43,920
Alright, I'll read the votes.

943
01:00:48,480 --> 01:00:50,560
First vote. David.

944
01:00:56,840 --> 01:00:58,520
David. That's two votes David.

945
01:01:03,760 --> 01:01:05,040
George.

946
01:01:06,240 --> 01:01:08,240
Two votes David, one vote George.

947
01:01:12,360 --> 01:01:14,240
George. We're tied.

948
01:01:14,240 --> 01:01:17,280
Two votes David, two votes George.

949
01:01:17,280 --> 01:01:18,440
One vote left.

950
01:01:29,560 --> 01:01:32,800
Second person voted out
of Australia Versus The World,

951
01:01:32,800 --> 01:01:34,320
David.

952
01:01:37,600 --> 01:01:39,240
I haven't had that many votes
since I won.

953
01:01:39,240 --> 01:01:40,640
What the heck?

954
01:01:42,040 --> 01:01:43,120
OK.

955
01:01:43,120 --> 01:01:44,800
(BOTH SPEAK INDISTINCTLY)

956
01:01:52,360 --> 01:01:53,840
I'm gonna take my time with this,

957
01:01:53,840 --> 01:01:57,160
because I think that's the last time
I ever play Australian Survivor.

958
01:01:57,160 --> 01:01:59,960
So, congratulations.
You guys retired me.

959
01:02:05,840 --> 01:02:08,360
Alright, David, the tribe has spoken.

960
01:02:10,200 --> 01:02:11,200
Beautiful.

961
01:02:11,200 --> 01:02:12,880
He needs a standing ovation.
It's the Golden God.

962
01:02:12,880 --> 01:02:14,080
(OTHERS AGREE)

963
01:02:18,440 --> 01:02:20,200
Alright. Thanks, guys.
See you, brother.

964
01:02:20,200 --> 01:02:21,520
Golden God out.

965
01:02:29,800 --> 01:02:32,320
Well, this tribe might be
full of relationships,

966
01:02:32,320 --> 01:02:34,760
but shack up with the wrong people,

967
01:02:34,760 --> 01:02:37,200
you might just find yourself dumped.

968
01:02:38,160 --> 01:02:39,960
Grab your torches, head back to camp.

969
01:02:39,960 --> 01:02:41,360
Goodnight.

970
01:02:43,280 --> 01:02:45,520
GEORGE: Whew! That was close.
LUKE: Yeah, it was close.

971
01:02:51,920 --> 01:02:53,160
Whew!

972
01:03:00,600 --> 01:03:01,720
The race is on.

973
01:03:04,520 --> 01:03:07,840
But who will open Pandora's box?

974
01:03:07,840 --> 01:03:09,200
TONY: These girls have a plan,

975
01:03:09,200 --> 01:03:12,160
and they don't want Tony
to throw a monkey wrench into it.

976
01:03:12,160 --> 01:03:13,680
And in that box
is probably a monkey wrench.

977
01:03:13,680 --> 01:03:16,160
And a growing pest problem...

978
01:03:16,160 --> 01:03:20,280
George does have tendencies
that a cockroach has.

979
01:03:20,280 --> 01:03:23,120
They're known to be
very hard to get rid of.

980
01:03:23,120 --> 01:03:24,880
..gets out of control.

981
01:03:24,880 --> 01:03:27,160
I'm bringing out
that bazooka from Bankstown.

982
01:03:29,560 --> 01:03:30,880
100%, Luke.

983
01:03:30,880 --> 01:03:34,360
Janine can get juiced.
Luke can get liquidated.

984
01:03:34,360 --> 01:03:36,880
I'm vengeful King George.

985
01:03:40,600 --> 01:03:43,160
Yeah, look, there's definitely
some solace in...

986
01:03:43,160 --> 01:03:46,080
No, I don't really play, so I'm...
I'm sour, you know?

987
01:03:46,080 --> 01:03:49,240
I don't take solace in nothing. I
wanted to stay in the game. (LAUGHS)

988
01:03:49,240 --> 01:03:52,560
But is there an honour
to be bestowed upon,

989
01:03:52,560 --> 01:03:54,240
like, the biggest threat
going out early?

990
01:03:54,240 --> 01:03:55,400
Yeah, maybe.

991
01:03:55,400 --> 01:03:57,800
I would have much preferred
to be still in there.

992
01:03:57,800 --> 01:04:00,840
It was, like, really down to
what Sarah was going to do.

993
01:04:00,840 --> 01:04:03,520
And...I don't know,
that was such a 50/50.

994
01:04:03,520 --> 01:04:06,400
And her saying she wanted to play
a loyalty game, I was like, "Bleah!"

995
01:04:07,400 --> 01:04:09,280
I don't know if she's watched
any of the newer seasons,

996
